  "generated_text": "Given the equation:\n\\[ e^{i \\alpha} + e^{i \\beta} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{3}{7} i \\]\n\nWe need to find \\( e^{-i \\alpha} + e^{-i \\beta} \\).\n\nFirst, recall that:\n\\[ e^{i \\theta} = \\cos \\theta + i \\sin \\theta \\]\n\\[ e^{-i \\theta} = \\cos \\theta - i \\sin \\theta \\]\n\nThus,\n\\[ e^{-i \\alpha} + e^{-i \\beta} = (\\cos \\alpha - i \\sin \\alpha) + (\\cos \\beta - i \\sin \\beta) \\]\n\nUsing the given equation:\n\\[ e^{i \\alpha} + e^{i \\beta} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{3}{7} i \\]\n\nWe get:\n\\[ e^{-i \\alpha} + e^{-i \\beta} = \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{3}{7} i \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{C}}\n\\]",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[c, '\\\\text{C}']",
    "gold_answer": "We can write\n\\[\\cos \\alpha + i \\sin \\alpha + \\cos \\beta + i \\sin \\beta = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{3}{7} i,\\]so $\\cos \\alpha + \\cos \\beta = \\frac{1}{4}$ and $\\sin \\alpha + \\sin \\beta = \\frac{3}{7}.$  Therefore,\n\\begin{align*}\ne^{-i \\alpha} + e^{-i \\beta} &= \\cos (-\\alpha) + i \\sin (-\\alpha) + \\cos (-\\beta) + i \\sin (-\\beta) \\\\\n&= \\cos \\alpha - i \\sin \\alpha + \\cos \\beta - i \\sin \\beta \\\\\n&= \\boxed{\\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{3}{7} i}.\n\\end{align*}",
    "is_correct": false
  },
